  artifactSprite: {fileID: 7940955985725703088, guid: de650d04e50a8524cb0da15df29ecf78, type: 3}
  plaqueTitle: ...
  plaqueDescription: A slender indigenous nose flute fashioned from mature mountain
    bamboo, played by blowing through a single nostril to produce gentle, haunting
    melodies during courtship and peaceful gatherings.
  artifactInspectionDescription: Carefully calibrated node holes drilled into seasoned
    mountain bamboo. The mouthpiece is angled smoothly, retaining natural lacquer
    from decades of ritual playing.
  initialDialogue: what should i do
  plaqueDialogue: what could this artifact be
  artifactDialogue: i wonder what this artifact looks like
  promptText: '[E] Inspect Artifact'
